================================================================================================
  ⭐⭐ THE ANSWER, and it is not a choice between estimators
================================================================================================
  The plug-in's bias is E|X-X'|/(2m) — it DIES AS 1/m. `(plug-fair)*m` above is flat
  within a few percent across m = 4 .. 1024, which is that signature.

  ⭐ And the sweep says something sharper than 'they converge': the FAIR estimator is
     already converged at m = 4. It is the PLUG-IN that moves.
  predictor                   plug-in m=4 plug-in m=1024   error at m=4
  soft_gate x NB body            0.054533       0.050089           8.9%
  NB body alone                  0.063205       0.047269          33.7%
                                 fair m=4    fair m=1024               
  soft_gate x NB body            0.050171       0.050072           0.2%
  NB body alone                  0.047729       0.047214           1.1%

  ⛔ WHAT IT COSTS THE RECORD. Published numbers were scored at m = 16.
  as published (m=16, plug-in)       margin NB body alone - soft_gate x NB body = -0.000216
  converged (m=1024, either)         margin NB body alone - soft_gate x NB body = -0.002858
  ⇒ the margin was understated 13x

  ⇒ ⭐ THERE IS NO ESTIMATOR DECISION HERE. There is a draw count to raise, and head draws
     are free (W-68). At m = 256 the two agree to under 0.0002 on both predictors.
  ⛔ The first version reported the m=16 gap as a decision for Simon. That was an
     unswept free parameter dressed as a finding — the exact error
     `feedback_sweep_before_reporting_a_scalar` exists for. Simon had already said so.

  ⚠️ WHAT REMAINS REAL: record numbers were computed at m=16 and carry the
     plug-in's 1/m bias, which differs PER ARM because it scales with that arm's own
     spread. For any cube storing mu/theta/gate this is re-scorable for free.

